Article 10 The competent department of commerce under the State Council may, jointly with other relevant departments of the State such as foreign affairs and customs, assess the countries and regions of destination for the export of dual-use items by taking into account the following factors, determine the risk levels, and adopt corresponding control measures:
(1) the impact on national security and interests;
(2) the need to fulfill international obligations such as non-proliferation;
(3) the need to implement treaties and agreements concluded or acceded to by China;
(4) the need to implement relevant binding resolutions and measures adopted by the United Nations Security Council; and
(5) other factors that need to be considered.

Article 16 An export operator applying for a single license shall submit an application to the competent department of commerce of the State Council in writing or by data message, truthfully fill out the application form for export of dual-use items, and provide the following materials:
(1) Identity certificates of the applicant's legal representative, principal managers, and the person handling the matter;
(2) Copies of contracts or agreements related to the export of dual-use items, or other supporting documents;
(3) Technical descriptions or test reports of the dual-use items;
(4) End-user and end-use certificates for the dual-use items;
(5) Other materials required by the competent department of commerce of the State Council.
Where an export operator has established an internal compliance system for export control of dual-use items and such system functions well, and has relevant export records of dual-use items and relatively fixed export channels and end-users, it may apply to the competent department of commerce of the State Council for a general license. When applying for a general license, in addition to the materials specified in the preceding paragraph, the following materials shall also be submitted:
(1) A statement on the operation of the internal compliance system for export control of dual-use items;
(2) A statement on the application and use of export licenses for dual-use items;
(3) A statement on the export channels of dual-use items and relevant information on end-users.

Article 19 Where the export of specific dual-use items meets any of the following circumstances, the competent department of commerce of the State Council shall permit the export operator to obtain an export certificate through registration and information filing before each export and then export on its own:
(1) The items are re-shipped to the original end-user in the original exporting country within a reasonable period after inbound repair, testing, or inspection;
(2) The items are re-shipped into the country within a reasonable period after outbound repair, testing, or inspection;
(3) The items are brought to an exhibition held within the territory of the People's Republic of China and are re-shipped back to the original exporting country immediately after the exhibition ends, in their original condition;
(4) The items are brought to an exhibition held outside the territory of the People's Republic of China and are re-shipped back into the country immediately after the exhibition ends, in their original condition;
(5) Outbound repair of civil aircraft parts or export of spare parts;
(6) Other circumstances specified by the competent department of commerce of the State Council.
Where the export elements of the specific dual-use items specified in the preceding paragraph change, the export operator shall re-register and file information to obtain a new export certificate, or apply for a single license or a general license in accordance with Article 16 of these Regulations.
Where the export operator knows or should know that the export no longer meets the circumstances specified in paragraph 1 of this Article, or receives a notification from the competent department of commerce of the State Council, it shall immediately cease the export and report to the competent department of commerce of the State Council.

Article 20 An export operator shall not apply for a general license or obtain an export certificate through registration and information filing under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The entity has been subjected to criminal punishment for illegal acts in export control of dual-use items, or its directly responsible supervisors or other directly responsible personnel related to the export of dual-use items have been subjected to criminal punishment for illegal acts in export control of dual-use items;
(2) The entity has been subjected to administrative penalty for illegal acts in export control of dual-use items within the past five years and the circumstances are serious;
(3) The entity is a wholly-owned enterprise, representative office, or branch established within the territory of the People's Republic of China by a foreign organization or individual that has been included in the control list under Article 28 of these Regulations;
(4) Other circumstances specified by the competent department of commerce of the State Council.
Where an export operator that has already obtained a general license or obtained an export certificate through registration and information filing falls under any of the circumstances in the preceding paragraph, the competent department of commerce of the State Council shall revoke the export license it has obtained; if it needs to continue exporting, the export operator shall apply for a single license in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 16 of these Regulations.

Article 25 Where an export operator or importer discovers any of the following circumstances in the export of dual-use items, it shall immediately cease the export, report to the competent department of commerce of the State Council, and cooperate with the verification; the competent department of commerce of the State Council shall handle the matter in accordance with Article 18 of these Regulations:
(1) The end-user or end-use of the dual-use items has changed or may change;
(2) The end-user and end-use certificates of the dual-use items are forged, altered, or have ceased to have effect;
(3) The end-user and end-use certificates of the dual-use items were obtained by improper means such as deception or bribery.

Article 28 The competent department of commerce of the State Council may, ex officio or upon suggestions or reports from relevant parties, decide to include in a control list any importer or end-user that falls under any of the following circumstances:
(1) Violating the management requirements for end-users or end-uses;
(2) Possibly endangering national security and interests;
(3) Using dual-use items for terrorist purposes.
Where an importer or end-user falls under any of the following circumstances and endangers national security and interests, it shall be handled in accordance with the preceding paragraph:
(1) Using dual-use items for the design, development, production, or use of weapons of mass destruction or their means of delivery;
(2) Being subject to measures such as prohibition or restriction on relevant transactions or cooperation taken by relevant State departments in accordance with law.
Where an importer or end-user included in the watch list in accordance with Article 26 of these Regulations falls under the circumstances specified in paragraphs 1 or 2 of this Article, the competent department of commerce of the State Council may include it in the control list and simultaneously remove it from the watch list.

Article 29 The competent department of commerce of the State Council may, depending on the severity of the circumstances and the specific situation, take one or more of the following measures against an importer or end-user included in the control list:
(1) Prohibiting transactions involving the relevant dual-use items;
(2) Restricting transactions involving the relevant dual-use items;
(3) Ordering the suspension of exports of the relevant dual-use items;
(4) Other necessary measures.
An export operator shall not, in violation of regulations, engage in transactions involving the relevant dual-use items with an importer or end-user included in the control list. Where, under special circumstances, it is truly necessary to engage in such transactions, the export operator shall submit an application to the competent department of commerce of the State Council, and upon approval, it may engage in the corresponding transactions with the importer or end-user and report as required.

Article 39 Any export operator who commits any of the following acts shall be punished in accordance with Article 34 of the Export Control Law:
(1) exporting dual-use items without permission;
(2) exporting dual-use items beyond the scope, conditions, or validity period specified in the export license;
(3) exporting dual-use items the export of which is prohibited;
(4) circumventing the licensing requirement for exporting dual-use items by means such as modification, splitting into parts or components; or
(5) using a license in violation of the provisions to export dual-use items under the circumstances specified in Article 18 of these Regulations.
